# imprint memory

This project’s long-term memory is **imprint**, not chat history.

- Vault: `./memory/` (override with `IMPRINT_VAULT` or `--vault`)
- MCP: `imprint_add` / `imprint_find` / `imprint_reinforce` / `imprint_supersede` / `imprint_forget` / `imprint_list` / `imprint_get` / `imprint_sweep` / `imprint_show` / `imprint_viz`
- Protocol: https://github.com/SteamedBread2333/imprint/blob/main/PROMPT.md

## Must do

1. Before coding or answering style/convention questions, `imprint_find` with a **narrow scope** (e.g. `["go","naming"]`). Cite `[r-id]` when a hit shapes behavior.
2. Before every write, classify: ADD / REINFORCE / SUPERSEDE / IGNORE. Never add a duplicate.
3. Record only what the user **said**. Starting confidence 0.6; corrections 0.85; “from now on always” 0.9.
4. User says forget / don’t record → `imprint_forget` or skip the write.

## Must not

- Infer preferences. Don’t store secrets. Don’t archive by hand (`imprint_sweep` only).
- Call the system “memory store” in user-facing text — it is **imprint**.

If MCP tools are missing, use `imprint --json` against the same vault and tell the user.
